  "parameter_rationale": "Three preregistered line sources: chart 1H/4H, completed 1D, completed 1W. For each, bounce and breakout each cover wing 3/5, deviation 2/4%, contact zone 0.5/1%, max age 50/100 source bars: 96 variants plus baseline. Both support and resistance and both trade directions are tested in every variant.",
  "min_bars": 100,
  "baseline": "One 25% long buy-and-hold position on the same stock and 1H/4H signal timeframe, filled next open; separately compare chart-source third touch against the existing two-pivot trendline-breakout experiment.",
  "signal_rule": "Two confirmed same-side ZigZag pivots on the selected chart, completed daily or completed weekly source define a projected support/resistance line. The higher-source pivot becomes usable only on the next date after its confirmation candle; no partial day/week is read. On the first later third contact, bounce enters away from the line after a rejecting close, or breakout enters through it after a beyond-zone close. Both support and resistance are eligible regardless of line slope. Ignore ambiguous simultaneous contacts and use each anchor pair once. Signal on completed 1H/4H close; fill next open; opposite signal closes/reverses.",
  "initial_capital_rub": 1000000,
  "position_weight_pct": 25,
